{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Good Leadership", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The GROW Model", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coach ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who trains a person or team", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: At each stage, the coach will ask relevant open questions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about the GROW model. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coachee", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who receives training from a coach", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The coach's questions are designed to help the coachee establish an appropriate objective.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coaching", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the activity of \u200bproviding \u200btraining for \u200bpeople or helping to prepare them for something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Professional coaching is a process of communication between a trained expert, or \"coach\", and a business executive, or \"coachee\". ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "context", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bsituation within which something \u200b\u200bhappens, and that can \u200bhelp \u200bexplain it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They should think about their objective in the context of the real world. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "action point", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a specific reason for action to be taken, typically one arising from a meeting", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The final stage of the this model is for the coach to ask the coachee questions that will help them identify some action points. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "put something into practice ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "start to use it and see if it is effective", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It is important to establish their willingness to put these actions into practice and move towards their goal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Purpose Clauses including To-Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " The most common way for you to express purpose is to use a<span class=\"strong\"> to-infinitive</span> (called an infinitive of purpose).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use<span class=\"strong\"> to-infinitive </span>(within a reason clause) especially when you want to express one particular purpose.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br><span class=\"italic\">I called to find out if she was still there</span>. <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Ben has gone into the city to do some research</span>. <br/><span class=\"italic\"> To get a good seat, you need to book ahead. </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'm writing to enquire about the availability of your staff</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "At this stage, the coach's questions are designed to help the coachee establish an appropriate objective.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This stage of the coaching conversation is all about helping the coachee to understand their present situation and to think about their objective in the context of the real world. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The GROW model describes four key areas to explore.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Intention and Willingness: <span class=\"italic\">Will </span>and <span class=\"italic\">Would</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to express intention to do something or a willingness to do something, you can use the verbs <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">will </span>and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">would.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Will</span> / <span class=\"strong\">Won't</span><br/>You use<span class=\"strong\"> will</span> / <span class=\"strong\">won't</span>  to express that someone is / is not  willing to do something in the present. <br/> Examples: <br><span class=\"italic\">Richard is a nice guy. He will always help you if you are in trouble. </span><br/><span class=\"italic\">Fernanda is mad at me; she will not (won't) talk to me. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Would</span> / <span class=\"strong\">Would not</span><br/> You use <span class=\"strong\"> would</span> / <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span>   to express that someone was / was not  willing to do something in the past. <br/>  Examples: <br></span><span class=\"italic\">My grandpa was such as nice man; he would always help people if they were in need. </span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">My teacher always helped me with unknown words, but he wouldn't translate the whole text. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "More examples: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Mary <span class=\"strong\">will </span>translate for you - she speaks French.</span> (willingness) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ll</span> do it - I don't mind. </span>(willingness) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">won't </span>be coming later. </span>(intention) <br/><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Would </span>you mind helping me, please? </span>(willingness) <br/><span class=\"italic\"> I'<span class=\"strong\">ll </span>call you later. </span>(intention)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the examples from the text. Keep the context in mind as you do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "At each stage, the coach will ask relevant open questions. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "These questions will encourage the coachee to reflect deeply.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How do you feel this process will help you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The coach will help the coachee explore the options that are available to them. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Work with a partner. One person is the coach and the other the coachee.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do the GROW model process and put your ideas on a poster.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "GOAL: Decide on a goal. Goals need to be SMART (specific, measurable, acceptable, realistic, timely).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "REALITY: Self-evaluate and identify the obstacles in your path.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "OPTIONS: Brainstorm ideas that can help solve your problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "WILL: Establish what is necessary to achieve your goals.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Switch roles with your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Next, present your posters to the class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm ideas with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create goals that are SMART.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I establish options and acknowledge the necessary steps needed to achieve these goals.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I facilitate my partner as they work through a GROW model.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my GROW model ideas to the class.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le06ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Professional coaching is a process of communication between a trained expert, or \"coach\", and a business executive, or \"coachee\". It is a popular way of improving business performance. The GROW model describes four key areas to explore. At each stage, the coach will ask relevant open questions. Each question forces the coachee to reflect deeply, achieve a better understanding of the situation in question, and start to identify some potential solutions.</br></br>Stage one - Goal:\nAt this stage, the coach's questions are designed to help the coachee establish an appropriate objective. The coach might ask some or all of the following questions: What do you want to achieve? How do you feel this process will help you? What do you think it will take for this process to be a success?", "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Stage two - Reality:\nThis stage of the coaching process helps the coachee to understand their present reality and think about their objective in the context of the real world. Questions from the coach might include: What challenges or obstacles do you expect to encounter? How will you overcome them?</br></br>Stage three - Options:\nThe coach will help the coachee explore the options that are available to them. Questions might include: What options are available to you? What are the pros and cons of each option?", "time": "52500"}, {"image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Stage four - Will/Way forward:\nIn the final stage of the this model, the coach will ask questions that help the coachee identify action points and establish their willingness to put these actions into practice and move towards their goal. Questions might include: How do you intend to put your chosen options into action? What does achieving your goal mean to you?</br></br>The GROW model establishes a framework for coaches to help coachees identify an objective, achieve a deeper understanding of the situation they face, explore the options that are available to them and identify an appropriate way forward. By asking open questions at each stage of the framework, the coach will facilitate, rather than direct, the conversation and, in doing so, will enable the coachee to arrive at their own conclusions.", "time": "89000"}], "coverimg": "engenn11le06ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can express willingness or intention to do something.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can report about the purpose of events or actions related to job issues.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about models in coaching.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you ever heard of the GROW model? What do you think it is about?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What do you think the GROW in the GROW model stands for?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "To grow or not to grow \u2026 that is the question!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " What are the four stages of the GROW model? How does this model help you <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">to achieve</span> your goals?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> \u201cTo achieve\u201d </span> means to successfully complete something by working hard.", "type": "text", "tip_id": 0}], "type": "tips"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "STI", "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}]}]}, {"id": 2, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\